      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: Luui",
        "size": "Medium",
        "name": "Changinc, Impersonator",
        "subname": "Rank 6 Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Changincs are a family of land-dwelling mollusks resembling octopuses that use camouflage and mimicry to hunt and defend themselves. Impersonators, the most common type of Changinc, are large cephalopods that use their ability to alter skin pigmentation and texture to deceive potential prey by mimicking other creatures. There are myths suggesting that these creatures can speak, and while this is true, they lack the intellect to form complex sentences, limiting themselves to repeating vocalizations they have previously heard.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 10
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 4
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Near ruins or settlements, Changinc Impersonators often disguise themselves as elements of their surroundings, like rocks, debris, or even parts of structures. They blend into shadows or cracks, perfectly imitating the textures and colors around them, which allows them to stealthily approach prey exploring the area. In hunting scenarios, they adopt shapes that evoke curiosity or a false sense of security. For instance, they may take on the appearance of creatures their prey finds harmless or familiar.\n\nChanginc Impersonators can roughly mimic the shape of other beings, which they use to either lure in or deceive predators and prey. In populated areas, they might vaguely imitate humans or other species, taking on familiar features (like ragged clothing or covered faces) that obscure their true forms. When threatened, they can use this ability to mimic a predator, discouraging attacks from other animals or unwary explorers.\n\nMore adept Impersonators can respond to questions or provoke short conversations, repeating phrases or sounds they've previously heard from travelers or local creatures. They use this skill to deceive curious explorers, luring them into dangerous or isolated areas. For example, they might emit cries for help or murmurs that echo through ruins, attracting adventurers into ambushes where other Changincs lie in wait, ready to capture or confuse their prey.\n\nWhen capturing prey with their tentacles, Changincs tend to restrain the target's movement and, if necessary, crush it slowly. However, if the situation turns unfavorable, they can quickly release the prey and retreat, hiding in a new position within the environment. This technique allows the Changinc to avoid direct confrontation, repositioning itself for a second attempt at capturing prey.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Although well-distributed throughout the Outer World, Impersonators are common in the Twilight Meridian, especially near ruins and settlements where the expansion of various peoples has allowed them to adapt to more specific impersonation tactics.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Portray Changincs as cunning creatures, moving slowly and carefully. They avoid direct confrontations, studying prey from afar and analyzing their environment before attacking. To convey this, pause before each action, creating a sense of tension as if the players are being watched.\r\n\r\nWhen roleplaying a Changinc\u2019s speech, use short phrases and repeat words or expressions they have previously heard. Keep the speech impersonal, almost like a recording, and adopt a flat or oddly placed tone as if the Changinc is \u201cacting\u201d without fully understanding what it's saying. This adds a disturbing, alien quality to their interactions.\r\n\r\nSince they\u2019re tentacled creatures, Changincs in imitated human or animal form will have slightly unsteady and clumsy movements. Describe hesitant steps, or even wet and irregular sounds as they try to mimic the gait of other creatures. This detail can make players sense something is \u201coff\u201d and feel uneasy while observing them.\r\n\r\nWhen a Changinc changes form, describe the transformation as liquid-like, with tentacles and body parts shifting and molding in a hypnotic way. Include subtle sounds of movement or a gradual fading from one color to another. This visual detail emphasizes their surreal, amorphous nature.\r\n\r\nWhen taking damage or being discovered, the Changinc may quickly revert to its true form or display desperate behavior. Describe the illusion of its form flickering, colors wavering, or a sudden return to tentacles, signaling its discomfort and vulnerability. This can be a good opportunity for players to notice the Changinc\u2019s weakness, balancing the challenge with a sense of tactical advantage.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "nnbpyq7yz3rmaPEnGC0H"
  },
