      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Varies",
        "name": "Copykitt",
        "subname": "Rank 0 Mook",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Scaredy tricksters. In many a dungeon or ancient ruin, both treasure and traps can be found. The well-known monsters known as Mimics disguise themselves as treasure to lure in unsuspecting adventurers. Their less well-known cousins, the Copykitts, instead disguise themselves as traps to ward off adventurers. Harmless and easily frightened, these sneaky creatures hide in plain sight. After all, what fool would willingly jump into a trap?",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 10
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 0
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Copykitts have one true strategy in life: look like something dangerous and hope nothing looks twice. If discovered, they will shriek in horror and attempt to escape. They prefer to escape by climbing walls and ceilings, hoping that whatever found them cannot follow. If cornered, they will cower in fear, sometimes trying desperately to change into a more frightening shape. None have ever been observed fighting.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "It's not currently known whether Copykitts can understand speech, but it's commonly believed that they cannot. They communicate with each other very rarely, preferring to remain silent as part of their disguise. On the rare occasions they make a sound, they will quietly click and squeak to each other. When discovered or otherwise startled, they are capable of a surprisingly loud terrified shriek.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Increase their Rank and give them more aggressive Abilities to create a more traditional Mimic.\n\nGiving them an Ability that lets them strike as if armed with a Concealed Weapon can turn them into a chameleon-like ambush predator. Alternatively, giving them an Ability that lets them inflict an Ailment on contact can turn them into a creature not unlike a stonefish.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Found all over the Outer World in various dungeons and ruins. While they can be found outside these usual haunts, they're considerably rarer and their disguises are often less convincing. Some rare specimens are able to disguise themselves as sinkholes, bramble bushes or other such natural hazards.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Suspiciously large numbers of traps in suspiciously obvious locations. Near-invisible dried slime trails. Tiny clicks and squeaks that suddenly stop after anyone makes any kind of noise.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Copykitts pretend to be traps, often keeping up appearances long after those observing have figured out the truth. They aren't always immobile traps, sometimes swinging from the ceiling to pretend to be a pendulum, or whirling across the floor pretending to be a saw blade. When touched or if anyone makes a threatening movement towards them, they shriek in terror and try to flee the scene. If they successfully escape, they will use their Perfect Mimicry Ability to try to disguise as another kind of trap. Unfortunately for them, the large amount of time this takes often leads to them being caught in the act by any persistent adventuring party. If the party question the trap or explicitly try to inspect it further, you should give small tells that it's not quite what it seems. Perhaps the pendulum axe has nowhere to slot into. Perhaps the spikes at the bottom of the pit are slightly droopy. Perhaps the rolling boulder is suspiciously smooth.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "Copykitts never carry anything usable. Very rarely they might set themselves up in a place that has something valuable, making it look as though an adventurer has perished to the deadly trap. Mostly though they set themselves up somewhere safe and away from everything else. A dead Copykitt's sticky slime can be used as a weak adhesive, which an enterprising scholar has used to create paper that may be easily stuck and removed from any workable surface, vastly improving organisation in scholarly environments. Otherworlders seem unimpressed by this innovation for some reason.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "W3px5s7eS02VvqM6cPCA"
  },
