      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "JDI5PNVLKTiiCBfIpGzT",
          "name": "Enemy Of Light [B][M].",
          "description": "Count Algebra is a creature of darkness and has supernatural powers over how it works in his presence. He may wrap himself in a cloak of darkness to better conceal his true form and may lash out with tendrils of darkness to assail his foes.\n\nHe may use even the barest shadows to wrap himself in darkness to conceal his true form. Even when in light he may draw the shadows cast by the flickering torchlight to wrap around himself in order to use Creature Of The Night. This requires him to make an Aura Check at the start of his Turn. On Failure, he still counts as being in darkness, but this uses up his Action for that Turn.\n\nHe can see perfectly in the dark without penalty and is immune to the Obscured Area Condition when caused by darkness.\n\nHe may wield shadows as a Lash Weapon that deals Dark Damage without needing to use his hands. If in light, he must make an Aura Check in order to do so, on failure he wastes his Action.\n\nLight from the Sun Machine, a Star Gem, or similarly powerful light sources completely nullifies this Ability while he is in it.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "QYf5TaZ5tihNWddJ3jLE",
          "name": "Miserable Pile Of Little Secrets [B].\nCount Algebra has the fa\u00e7ade of a powerful Immortal, such as the Duke of Red Roses. However, while he really is an Immortal, his true form is far from intimidating. Keeping this secret has also taught him how to uncover the secrets of others.\n\nThis functions identically to the Heretic's Ability Dreadful (Page 69 of the BREAK!!",
          "description": "Rulebook)",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "ht8rlzN1fhjVZKn3IHLG",
          "name": "Wielder Of Fear [A][M].",
          "description": "As master of fear and shadow, Count Algebra can wield fear as a terrifying weapon.\n\nHe may target anyone whose fear he has identified through Miserable Pile Of Little Secrets from up to 2 Areas away, who must then make a Grit Check. On Failure they receive a vision of their greatest fear attacking or otherwise harming them. If there is no such valid way for this to happen, then something representing this fear attacks them instead. For example, if they fear failure they might see a vision of someone they care about attacking them as a consequence of their failure.\n\nThe Target becomes Terrified of Count Algebra. If they are already Terrified, they suffer a Snag on this Check and take 2 Hearts of Dark Damage on failure.\n\nIf Count Algebra's True Form Revealed Ability is triggered, anyone who witnesses his true form recovers from the Terrified Ailment caused by this Ability immediately.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "vf4v4HxSNG9Ir0H0ROqe",
          "name": "Creature Of The Night [L][M].",
          "description": "Darkness is Count Algebra's ally. The shadows protect him and keep him from truly dying.\n\nCount Algebra has an Edge on all Aura Checks and Contests.\nCount Algebra is immune to Dark Damage.\nWhile in darkness, Count Algebra has the following:\n- +2 to Defence Rating\n- Reduces Damage from all sources except Bright Damage by 1 Heart\n- Recovers 1 Heart per Turn\n- If defeated, after spending 3 Turns in total darkness, he revives at maximum Hearts\n\nAdditionally, while in darkness, he can call upon the shadows to transport him. Instead of moving normally, he can choose to collapse into a living shadow, move up to two Battlefield Areas away, then reform. In this form he can go anywhere a shadow could, such as fit under a tiny crack or even pass through a solid pane of glass. However, he is blocked by anything opaque, even if he could easily push it aside in his regular form. If he has not yet spent an Action this turn, he can still make an Action after doing this.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "Do4KtVUv38cDPPZLWrLp",
          "name": "True Form Revealed [B][M].",
          "description": "Count Algebra is a fearsome foe...in the darkness. When in the light of the Sun Machine, all can see him for what he really is. A small, pathetic, puppet-like creature.\n\nWhen in the light from the Sun Machine, a Star Gem, or similarly powerful light sources anyone that can see him sees his true form. Furthermore, anyone who has ever seen his true form will forever see his true form, even if he returns to darkness.\n\nHis true form is Small size, so adjust his Defence Rating and Attributes accordingly. Additionally, anyone who can see his true form cannot negatively be affected by any of his other Abilities.\n\nIf there's ever a situation where some of a group have seen his true form and some have not, while you could calculate his Attributes and Defence Rating based on the specific person involved in the interaction, for simplicity's sake treat him as Small size.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ],
