      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Medium*",
        "name": "Count Algebra",
        "subname": "Rank 5 Mega-Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Felt fright. In the darkest corners of Outer World, lit only by flashes of dramatic lightning, resides the dreaded Count Algebra. Wicked to the extreme, he is an incarnation of terror, a fearful avatar of horror, and is really, truly scary...at least, to those who have never seen him. Once the veil of fear is torn away upon witnessing his true form, none can take him seriously again.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 13
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "lZyOvJ6Ou15Njc19IslC",
            "itemId": "csuMH93zCUtXAFfMLIyu",
            "name": "Count Algebra's Rapier",
            "description": "An exceptionally well-made sword, forged of Shade Iron and exquisitely designed to match the sensibilities befitting a noble such as himself.\nA Combination Master/Quick Weapon made from Shade Iron. While the blade itself has no magical abilities, if a Forger Imbues it with anything darkness-themed (Dark Damage, causing Blindness, etc) they gain an Edge on their Crafting Check due to the Dark mana it has absorbed while in his possession. The GM is final arbiter of what counts as darkness-themed.",
            "type": "none",
            "privacy": {
              "level": "public",
              "users": []
            },
            "creator": "",
            "data": {
              "cost": {
                "coins": 400
              },
              "encumbrance": 2.0
            },
            "version": 0,
            "owners": [],
            "quantity": 1,
            "equipped": false,
            "isCustom": true,
            "actions": []
          }
        ],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 4
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "He will usually face the party alone, or with a minimum of mooks if this isn't feasible. Many of his mooks, including those encountered before reaching him, are armed with weapons known as \"Snuffers\", which are long poles ending with a bell or clamp-shaped contraption. These are to be treated as Lash Weapons with an Edge on any rolls specifically used to snuff out, destroy, or knock away light sources.\n\nFocus on remaining in the dark, snuffing out light sources the party bring with them. His lair also contains traps that snuff out light sources, such as waterfall traps or gusts of wind. If he even suspects the party have a Star Gem, he will ensure they don't draw it or, failing that, will flee.\n\nHe will keep his distance and attempt to identify the party's fears, lashing them with shadow tendrils if they get too close. After identifying the party's fears, he will attempt to Terrify them one by one, though he will also do this before identifying the whole party's fears if a particular party member keeps getting too close. Once everyone is terrified, he will pummel them with Wielder Of Fear. \n\nIf his True Form Revealed Ability is triggered, he will assess the situation. If he thinks he stands a chance, he'll attempt to silence the witnesses. Most likely though, he'll try to flee and take up residence in a different region of Wistful Dark. ",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Combat Gear",
          "id": "AdV2VUGGxlLp3oS0OFPO",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "description": "He also wears fairly standard (if fancy) Light Armour, sized for a Small Creature, if the party wish to strip him of it. This armour satisfies the conditions to be used without penalty for someone with the Stylish Quirk.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "combat-gear",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Count Algebra has lived countless centuries and as such has picked up a number of languages. While he prefers Dark Tongue, he can speak all the languages available to the Wistful Dark. It's plausible he speaks other languages too, so optionally you may have him speak one additional language, perhaps one relevant to the party that he may surprise them with.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "By removing or severely altering True Form Revealed you can make a much more serious and deadly vampire-like creature. Count Algebra is intended to at first come across as serious, but then be revealed as silly so this will drastically alter the intended tone, but could make for a very interesting boss fight.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Count Algebra can be found in one of his towers, spread throughout Wistful Dark. He has multiple haunts and tends to abandon one and return to another whenever he is found out.\n\nWhile the Count himself doesn't tend to carry much on him, his towers contain numerous items that may be looted. As he has spent many centuries collecting curios, the GM is free to populate anything they see fit. ",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Unless something has gone horribly wrong and he bumps into the party on the road while fleeing another group that triggered True Form Revealed, Count Algebra will never be encountered outside of one of his towers and therefore will always be encountered passively yet purposefully.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "While cloaked in shadow, he appears as a tall, suave, lordly figure. Fear is his ally and he can use it to cause very real harm to his foes. Even those who can see perfectly in the dark see only a shadowy silhouette of this lordly figure. When bathed in enough light that he is unable to hide even the smallest detail, his true form is revealed: that of a small, fuzzy being akin to a puppet. While he is still malevolent in this form, he is considerably less dangerous. What's worse (for him) is once his true form is witnessed, it is no longer possible for him to hide his form from witnesses, even if he returns to darkness.\n\nHowever, he is truly immortal and cannot be permanently destroyed by any force in Outer World. He can be kept in a state of death by keeping his remains in light but eventually, either by the light sources failing or by a loyal minion or na\u00efve bystander moving his body to darkness, he will return to life no worse for wear. Perhaps an exceedingly powerful being may know of a way to put a permanent end to him...",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "Dark Pendant.\nA golden chain with a large black diamond which hung low from Count Algebra's neck. While the gem can be removed and spent as any other gem, this devalues the jewellery as a whole. The chain itself is only worth a few Coins, depending on the buyer, but can be sold separately if necessary.\n\nAs the gem has spent a considerable length of time in Count Algebra's possession, it has absorbed some of his Dark mana. As such, it may be treated as an Element Gem with the Dark element.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "Axx5n3xxSmWRxccpDH0B"
  },
