      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: ichiCharmed [Discord]",
        "size": "?",
        "name": "Crystalline Dreg",
        "subname": "Rank 2 Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Maybe not a girl\u2019s best friend. Once humanoid creatures whose physical forms have been warped into hard crystal due to phenomena involving arcane energies or experimentation with mana. They have the innate ability to pull in light and other elements before firing them back out as beam attacks towards their enemies.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 16
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 2
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Being quite the literal glass cannon, the Crystalline Dreg will prefer to:\n- Stay behind sturdier allies and blast foes from afar with its beams\n- Only \u201ctank\u201d elemental damage to alter its attacks\n- Flee from foes that attack with blunt/bludgeoning weapons\n- Otherwise focus on other melee focused enemies\n- Flee if tankier allies are defeated or if severely outnumbered\n",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "You can allow the Crystalline Dreg to absorb other Special Damage types as well if you wish to give your party more of a challenge and the Dreg more variety in its toolset.\r",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Refracted light moving closer and closer, soft groaning, the sound of crystals dragging against the ground\r",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Simple and cowardly beasts, they are drawn to large sources of contamination, arcane or otherwise, including living creatures and will attack small enough groups of people if they are spotted.\r\n",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "Sentient Shard.\nA shard broke off from the Dreg\u2019s crystalline form, refracting colors that could be described as beautiful, if not for the screaming faces also reflecting across the shard\u2019s surface. Creepy.\nAttack: Imbued Melee Weapons are given the ability to release bolts of blinding light like a Thrown Weapon, forcing a creature to make a Deftness Check in order to avoid being Blinded if struck. Obviously, these bolts do Bright Damage.\n\nDefense: Imbued items are given the ability to absorb Frost, Flame, Lightning, or Bright Damage once per Fight, giving the one wearing the item a Reduction of 1 Damage to that Type for one Turn.\n\nNote: If an adventurer were to both wear a Melee Weapon and a shield/piece of armor imbued by a Sentient Shard, the abilities listed above would work in tandem, allowing the imbued weapon to inflict whatever Special Damage type was absorbed by the shield/armor on top of the damage reduction.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "Yfv5Hycfou2Nbk67s4ZF"
  },
