          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Primarily with loud roars, low growls and crocodilian hisses. Nobody has yet managed to tame one so it is unknown if they could be trained to understand speech.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Rumours of extremely rare magical mutations of Dominatelio Anax have never been proven or disproven, but are persistent. Perhaps they are extremely susceptible to magic which is where their infamous hatred comes from. The rumours often feature such a beast breathing fire like a dragon or firing sharp spines at opponents. Some even rumour that there exists a two-headed monster, able to bite multiple enemies at once, though surely this is just the overactive imagination of a bored peasantry?\n\nTheir statistics and Abilities can be tweaked to represent other large dinosaurs. For example, granting them the ability to swim better could simulate a spinosaurus while increasing their speed could simulate a Utahraptor.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Native to Blazing Garden, especially the rainforests of Taaga, but can potentially be found anywhere there is a forest large enough to support it. They require an enormous amount of meat daily, so regions with little to no prey will not be able to support them.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Crushed foliage, large footprints, loud roaring in the distance, puddles or other still water rippling in time with stomping sounds.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Despite their monstrous appearance, Dominatelio Anax are still animals. They have reasonable animalistic motivations such as food, shelter and territory. The only exception to this is their extreme hatred of magic. Once a magic-user has used a Magical Ability against them, this hatred overrides all other animal instincts.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "csyIipVBoiYyfK0pt3jr"
  },
