          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "The Drakkenheim Sewer Gator is primarily aquatic and terrifyingly cunning, meaning it will:\r\n- Stick to the water when fighting and hunting\r\n- Single out weaker prey first, dragging them into the water with a powerful bite and finishing them off with Death Roll\r\n- Flees the fight once it drops below half Hearts\r\n",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "It seems to understand Low Speech, but pays it little heed as it lunges towards its next meal.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Remove the sewer gator\u2019s Predator Stealth and Death Roll and replace them with the Chompa\u2019s Blubbery Hide for an even tankier, mutated version of the monster.\r\n\r\nYou can also take Contaminated Regeneration and place it on creatures that live in contaminated/polluted environments, from fish and birds and more!\r\n\r\n",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "The Sewer Gator, hence its name, lives primarily in the sewers of whatever region it unfortunately calls home.\r",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Rumbling growls, ridged spines cutting through water, pale skin barely visible in darkness\r",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Cunning but certainly no geniuses, the Drakkenheim Sewer Gator can be agitated out of the water with enough persuasion (or food). They\u2019re still beasts, after all.\r",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ]
