      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Small",
        "name": "Glass Skitter",
        "subname": "Rank 0 Mook",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Crystal Creep. A beautiful glass sculpture of the eight-legged vermin found across the Outer World. Just as you start to admire it, it skitters towards you, ready to attack! Formed out of the excess mana from Ignis and Terra in the Heart Of Glass, this Growl-sized construct performs menial tasks in the lab. Lugging equipment, performing light repairs and defending against intruders are innate to them.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 12
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 0
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Glass Skitters will attempt to ambush foes, especially in numbers. A favourite tactic seems to be dropping from the ceiling onto an intruder and attempting to bite it to death before it can react. In large numbers they exhibit surprisingly competent strategy, with groups acting as decoys or hampering a foe's movement while another group goes in for the kill.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Glass Skitters make a curious chittering sound which they appear to use communicate with each other. They also understand High Akenian, but have no means of speaking it.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Increase their Rank and give them a Ranged Attack to represent a rare mutation known as a Shard Spitter.\n\nRemoving Born Of Mana and adding some kind of web shooting Ability can create the classic giant spider. Consider also increasing their rank and adding a venomous property to their bite and you can get an even better instance of this.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Found exclusively in Ignis and Terra's laboratory in a forgotten corner of the Buried Kingdom. They are constantly working. If there's no equipment to lug, they make minor repairs. There's no repairs needed, they patrol for intruders. If removed from the lab, they would need a considerable amount of time to find a new role, but could theoretically be tamed or go feral as they have no inherent loyalty to their creators.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "The plinkplinkplink of glass legs skittering on a hard surface, small scratches on hard surfaces, tidy workstations despite the knowledge that Ignis and Terra are fairly disorganised.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Glass Skitters act similar to a regular Skitter, acting as ambush predators towards the intruders to Ignis and Terra's laboratory. When not patrolling for intruders, they exhibit more purposeful behaviour, such as performing odd jobs around the laboratory such as tidying, repairing or disposing of waste. The rare feral Glass Skitter that has been away from the lab long enough to forget its purpose is an extremely territorial predator, made all the more unnerving by the fact it does not eat its victims but rather appears to simply collect their corpses. Those even rarer few who have been successfully tamed are restless, constantly looking for something to do. They are eager to follow orders, but will sometimes get up to mischief in the guise of protecting its master.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "When killed, a Glass Skitter shatters into countless shards of glass. Unless you find someone willing to buy broken glass, you're not likely to get anything out of it. If you manage to dispel the mana keeping them alive though, you may be able to sell an intact Glass Skitter as an art piece which could be worth a few coins depending on the buyer.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "EPD3KzLfqTko4K2Hn6Np"
  },
