      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "7MjzX3mY0lOwB0BR7YpY",
          "name": "Fastest Cephalopod In The Buried Kingdom [B].",
          "description": "A Glocktopus is a large fleshy body with eight tentacles that end in a curious barrel-shaped hole vaguely resembling that of a firearm. Through biological functions that are not yet fully understood, the creature creates ammunition and a black powder-like material. From there, it acts very much like a manufactured firearm and strikes with alarming precision.\n\nMay make Attacks with its Tentacles as though armed with Combination Standard/Light Mechanical Missile Weapons. As long as it has at least 2 Tentacles left, it is always considered to be Dual-Wielding, but must use the same type of Attack as its follow-up, meaning it cannot follow-up with a Ranged Attack if it does not have enough ammunition left. Each Tentacle has 1 shot before it needs to Reload, though you should not worry about tracking the specific tentacles and just track the number of shots fired.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "fyqW0XhIfbsd2aK0xdKe",
          "name": "Biological Ammunition [A].",
          "description": "The Glocktopus has never been studied in full and so we have gaps in our knowledge of how these beasts work. What we do know is they are able to create ammunition for their strange biological firearms at an astonishing rate.\n\nConsidered to have unlimited ammo for Fastest Cephalopod In The Buried Kingdom.\nWhen Reloading, it Reloads all of its Tentacles in one Action.\nIf in Water when it performs its Reload, it gains a Minor Bonus to its Defence Rating by taking cover underwater.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "DA4pXofTBl3hYqtPxcQ7",
          "name": "Creature From The Buried Lake [A].",
          "description": "Being a water-dwelling beast that dwells underground has some advantages.\n\nCan breathe water, so is immune to the Suffocating Area Condition caused specifically by being submerged in water. Some kind of material or effect that removes or displaces the oxygen levels in water may remove this immunity. \n\nIt may survive outside of water unhindered for one hour. After that it must make a Grit Check every hour. Failure reduces its maximum Hearts Total by 1 and it dies if it reaches 0. It restores its Hearts total when fully submerged in water for one minute per Heart lost.\n\nFast while in water, Slow while fully out of water. Its Speed is based on where it was when it began its turn, its Defence Rating is based on where it is when it receives an Attack.\n\nReceives a Minor Bonus to any roll involving being stealthy while submerged in water.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "6WZ2m4b7Ayl0LLxCG0u4",
          "name": "Rubbery Body [B].",
          "description": "A Glocktopus' rubbery flesh and squishy nature provides some measure of defence.\n\n- +2 Defence Rating\n- +1 Hearts Total\n- Crushing and squashing Attacks, such as fists or clubs, deal one less Damage",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "P59Oq8MXXRfkEoK758ro",
          "name": "Tentacled Terror [L].",
          "description": "Being a beast of many limbs, the Glocktopus is a whirlpool of destruction in combat.\n\nAfter performing an Attack Action, the Glocktopus immediately makes another Attack Action for free against a single different Target with Fastest Cephalopod In The Buried Kingdom as long as it still has enough remaining tentacles that have not Attacked this Round.\nIf after this second Attack Action it has any remaining tentacles that have not Attacked this Round, it waves them wildly in a defensive pattern, gaining a Minor Bonus to its Defence Rating.\n\nWhen attacking the Glocktopus, the Attacker may choose to attack a Tentacle instead of the body, though this decision must be made before rolling. A Glocktopus has eight Tentacles by default and is Incapacitated when it reaches 0. Each Tentacle has the benefit of Rubbery Body and has the following stats:\n- 12 Defence Rating\n- 1 Hearts Total (using the default assumption that creature limbs usually have 0 Hearts and instead that damage is removed from the creature it is attached to)\n\nTentacles are not affected by Attacks that hit multiple Targets, unless that Attack is aimed specifically at the Tentacle. In this case, only that specific Tentacle is affected. A Tentacle may not make any Checks or Contests, as the Glocktopus itself must make them. The GM may decide what is reasonable in a specific situation and may rule that the Glocktopus may avoid doing the Check or Contest entirely for an effect that affects only a Tentacle if it makes sense.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ],
