        ],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 5
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "The Glocktopus is an ambush predator. As such it will always attempt to take the party by surprise and may decide to simply leave without a fight if it notices that it has been noticed. While in fights it will try to use every advantage it can and will flee if the fight is too far against it. It prefers to use its Ranged Attacks, falling back on its Melee Attacks only when necessary. It can and will use Attack Stunts to increase the range of its Attacks, but if there is a closer Target it will normally go for them first. It will go on land only as a last resort and will usually seek to get back into water as quickly as possible.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Glocktopus communicate with each other via body language and subtle colour changes. It is not believed that they can understand speech and they have never been documented making any sounds, excluding the incidental sounds of them moving through water and the thunderous crack of their biological firearms.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Increase its Rank, grant it immunity to a specific type of Special Damage and grant its Ranged Attacks that same Special Damage to create rare elemental subspecies of Glocktopus.\n\nRemoving its Ranged Attacks and replacing them with a kind of inky special attack can create a more traditional cephalopod foe. Alternatively, adding on mechanical traits can create a steam-powered submersible war machine from Old Iron.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "They live and hunt in the numerous underground lakes in the Buried Kingdom and are sometimes also found in the underground rivers, usually when travelling between lakes for one reason or another. They can survive outside of the Buried Kingdom, but will not willingly venture there. On the surface, the only place they're likely to be comfortable is Wistful Dark. If they find themselves in Blazing Garden they likely will not survive for long.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "The sound of gunfire piercing the silence with a curious lack of battle cries or other indicators of war, the occasional inky trail of black powder mixed with water, the smell of gunpowder with a fishy hint.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "A silent hunter, the Glocktopus rarely attacks foes that are aware of it. Outside of combat, it acts much like any other ordinary aquatic animal.\n\nThe Glocktopus' name seems to be considered \"too on the nose\" by Other Worlders, suggesting there is a type of firearm in the Other World known as a \"Topus\". To satisfy curious Other Worlders reading this entry, the Glocktopus gets its name from New Ore slang. One of the many, many slang fads in New Ore history involved coining words that rhymed with Rock. Stealing became \"Twock\", junk became \"Schlock\", firearms became \"Glock\" and so on. This creature was discovered during this phase and, because of the firearm-like appendages the creature has, it became nicknamed the Glocktopus which eventually became the official name of the species.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "ZzU72Xs2RA3cfdPrZM0F"
  },
