          "displayName": "Stomping Feet"
        }
      ],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "GHw82zf2qtt06guVvZoD",
          "name": "Towering Terror [B].",
          "description": "An enormous beast of chitin and fury. \n\n- Hiratagaan is Massive.\n- Sweep Attack: Slashing tail counts as an Arc Weapon.\n- Focus Attack: Pounding fists and stomping feet count as Mighty Weapons.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "m61PYJ7EsDtqTRbWO1nB",
          "name": "Callous Carapace [B].",
          "description": "Hiratagaan's chitinous carapace is exactly as tough as it looks.\n\n+6 Defence Rating",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "CybBxdGJsi1tvo7CNUIf",
          "name": "Phantom Abomination [L][M].",
          "description": "Hiratagaan was dreamed into existence aeons ago, before the current laws of reality were set. As such, its connection to the material world is tenuous at best. Physical and magical attacks alike pass harmlessly through it as though it was not there. When it strikes back, it solidifies into a physical form just long enough to cause harm to its target, then returns to a state of intangibility.\n\nAny Attack, Ability, object or effect passes harmlessly through Hiratagaan. Do not even roll to see if it hits, it simply misses automatically. Hiratagaan does not need to make any Check or Contest for such things, counting as automatically winning them. While intangible, Hiratagaan can simply pass through solid objects, though it prefers to physically smash them anyway.\n\nThere are two ways to bypass this immunity:\n- Using the React Action to target Hiratagaan the moment it Attacks another allows the user to make a Deftness vs Deftness Contest against Hiratagaan. If they Succeed they can attack and damage it as normal. If they Fail, they were a moment too slow and Hiratagaan has become intangible again just before the attack hit. If the user is the current Target(s) of Hiratagaan's attack, they receive a Minor Bonus on this Contest.\n- If a creature spends its turn playing a musical instrument within earshot of Hiratagaan, Phantom Abomination is disabled until the beginning of that creature's next turn, where they may choose to continue to spend a turn playing. If the instrument being played is a wind instrument, Hiratagaan is also Terrified while the instrument is being played.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "Viq7jNlXoyEQjY0Ao24d",
          "name": "Wrath Of The Dragon [A][M].",
          "description": "Adding to the already-formidable beast's destructive prowess, its trump card is a powerful blast of fire it can spout from its mouth. One swift blast can cause widespread devastation.\n\nHiratagaan may use Wrath Of The Dragon to target one Area adjacent to the one it currently occupies.\n\nEverything in the targeted Area must make a Deftness Check or take 1 Flame Damage. A man-sized crater is left at the point of impact and every unattended flammable object is set on fire. At the GM's discretion, the crater may alter the Area in some way such as opening a path or causing an archway to collapse.\n\nHiratagaan may use this once per Combat safely. If it wishes to use this again in the same Combat, it expends a Heart to do so.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ],
