      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Massive",
        "name": "Hiratagaan",
        "subname": "Rank 6 Mega-Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Phantom Destroyer. A towering terror and one that represents pure destructive potential. Hiratagaan is a loyal minion of Bellzuub, though it's not known whether it obeys due to zeal or bloodlust. While Bellzuub is known for their subtlety, they acknowledge that sometimes it pays to have a giant rampaging monster to solve certain problems. Perhaps the most frightening thing of all about it is its complete intangibility, which it maintains until the very moment it strikes. This tiny window to strike back against it makes it impervious to most forms of attack.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 14
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "jUBqjCdwAxiUaSZTMOBi",
            "itemId": "0y9rj2ztEaJFZRvd5rdo",
            "name": "The Heart Of Hiratagaan",
            "description": "With the proper Ability, Hiratagaan's heart may be cut out once it is slain. Its heart is made from some kind of clay-like Magical Material, is shaped curiously like an ocarina and, once cleaned thoroughly, may be played like one too. While playing a song in major key, insects, arachnids and similar creatures are fascinated and may only watch you, unless disturbed or attacked. While playing a song in minor key, those same creatures are Terrified while within earshot. A sentient creature that would otherwise be affected may make a Grit or Aura Check to ignore the effect.",
            "type": "none",
            "privacy": {
              "level": "public",
              "users": []
            },
            "creator": "",
            "data": {
              "cost": {
                "coins": 150
              },
              "encumbrance": 1.0
            },
            "version": 0,
            "owners": [],
            "quantity": 1,
            "equipped": false,
            "isCustom": true,
            "actions": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ONls9n8hcdNVcibnMyWv",
            "itemId": "uM4GdDZXrAJ0hoVWVgpp",
            "name": "Hiratagaan's Blood",
            "description": "With the right Ability, up to three units of Hiratagaan's Blood may be harvested. This pungent, thick yellow liquid can be used as a Crafting Additive.\nEldritch: For up to one hour after consuming the imbued food or potion, you gain the Phantom Abomination Ability. If a wind instrument is used to bypass your intangibility, the feeling that you are being unravelled from the inside out wells up inside you inexplicably, which gives you the Terrified Ailment regardless of your musical tastes.",
            "type": "none",
            "privacy": {
              "level": "public",
              "users": []
            },
            "creator": "",
            "data": {
              "cost": {
                "coins": 50
              },
              "encumbrance": 1.0
            },
            "version": 0,
            "owners": [],
            "quantity": 1,
            "equipped": false,
            "isCustom": true,
            "actions": []
          }
        ],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 6
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Hiratagaan has all the tactical acumen of a rampaging beast. It lives to destroy and doesn't much care how it brings this about. It does however recognise the value in Attack Stunts, sometimes attempting to either grab foes in its giant fists or crush them beneath its tail. It reserves its Wrath Of The Dragon Ability to situations where it can cause the most devastation. Whether this means \"most foes in an Area\" or simply \"most smashable and/or flammable objects in an area\" depends wildly on whim.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Hiratagaan is only ever heard roaring in pure fury. It is unknown if it can understand speech at all, but Bellzuub is known to be able to communicate with it. It's not known whether this is through a language or simply due to Bellzuub's ability to speak with insects.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Grant it an Insectoid Aspect or two from Bellzuub's entry, to increase its options.\n\nFor a much more deadly foe and one closer to the source inspiration, after death describe Hiratagaan as appearing to turn to stone. After allowing the party one turn, Hiratagaan bursts from its cocoon stronger than before. Restore it to full Hearts and grant it two Insectoid Aspects (Barbed Appendage and Fluttering Wings are closest to the source inspiration, but rolling for both can create an interesting twist) before resuming the fight on its turn. For the purposes of Wrath Of The Dragon, treat this as a new Combat.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Can be found wherever Bellzuub points it. Its phantom aspect makes it easy to manifest wherever its master pleases.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Rage-filled roars echoing in the distance, a trail of destruction, the smell of smoke and blood.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
