              "value": 6,
              "visible": true
            },
            "deftness": {
              "value": 6,
              "visible": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Tiny*",
        "name": "Klikabrik",
        "subname": "Rank 0 Mook",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Combining combatants. A cube of metal, about 50cm in all dimensions, hovers before you, patrolling the forgotten techruin corridor you're exploring. It spots you and electrifies itself, charging into you which stings a bit, but is otherwise harmless. You turn to see another. And another. And another. They begin to combine with a magnetic click before slamming into you again, causing intense electrical pain to course through your body. Not so harmless after all...",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 13
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 1
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Klikabriks are never far from more Klikabriks. In a fight they'll often use Combat Tricks and Attack Assists to aid allies if they happen to be alone. When together, they'll try to combine as quickly as possible so as to be more effective in battle. As the individual Klikabriks are quite fragile, this can sometimes make them easier to deal with. As they grow in size, it's easier to hit them, so take advantage where you can and don't allow them to combine too much.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Klikabriks exclusively speak and understand Gleysian Code.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Increase their Speed Rating and allow their Charged Attack to function as a Quick Weapon to get a Scout Model.\n\nRemoving Magnetic Merging and treating Charged Attack as a Small Mechanical Missile Weapon can create a tiny sentry bot. In this case, ignore the rule that Tiny Adversaries can't hurt larger opponents to make them a credible threat or make them use Combat Tricks instead to simulate stun guns and the like.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Found in the techruins that litter the Outer World, especially in Stahlfield, where they patrol unceasingly. Occasionally found outside of these where they'll often act as though they're still in a techruin by trying to do illogical things such as attempting to recharge by plugging into a tree.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "A faint electrical hum, electrical devices having minor malfunctions, an odd trail of metallic objects.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Orderly and territorial. They defend the techruin (or whatever they think is a techruin if they've been displaced) fiercely, letting none pass through. While patrolling, those that can understand Gleysian Code can hear them calling to each other with military-like patrol reports. If captured and interrogated, they respond as a prisoner of war would: monotonously giving out their make, model and serial number then being frustratingly silent. Those that can appeal to their military nature may find them much friendlier, if in an army banter manner.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "When a Klikabrik is destroyed, it's usually smashed into bits, rendering anything potentially useful unsalvageable. If the attacker is specifically trying not to cause too much damage so as to try to scavenge some parts, they may take a Minor Penalty to their Attack to do so. Anyone with the Gadgeteering Crafting Discipline or a Purview relevant to ancient technology can attempt to scavenge something useful from a Klikabrik defeated in such a way, resulting in useful scrap to a value decided by the GM.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "YRQn7iCKavUs4VewGYFx"
  },
