      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Large",
        "name": "Kranky Klaws",
        "subname": "Rank 8 Mega-Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Festive horror. Festivals are an integral part of the Outer World, with celebrations for a wide variety of reasons being excuses for bringing people of all kinds together. Nobody likes festivals more than Kranky Klaws, sometimes referred to in hushed whispers as The Krankus. It is not known where or when he will strike, but he is always found where festivals are happening. With his Bag Of Gifts, it's a flip of a coin whether he'll give you something naughty or nice... or take you as his own gift.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 15
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 8
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "He keeps a so-called Naughty & Nice List and appears to focus on those he deems to be on the Naughty List. Kranky Klaws ignores anyone on the Nice list entirely. If all conscious Party Members are on the Nice List Kranky Klaws will use his Actions to hand Treats to them one by one. If they all accept the Treats and don't do anything to get themselves removed from the Nice List then he will use the Flee Action. Given the choice, he will always Attack someone on the Naughty List. He will prioritise putting Bright-aligned creatures in his Bag Of Gifts, assuming they are not on the Nice List. Ignore the Naughty and Nice List if it does not suit your Saga or if it is too much work.\n\nDark-aligned people are always on the Naughty List. Anyone with 2 or more Naughty Points are on the Naughty List. Anyone with -3 or less Naughty Points are on the Nice List.\nBright-aligned creatures have -3 Naughty Points. Twilight-aligned creatures have +1 Naughty Points. Large or larger creatures have +1 Naughty Points. Small or smaller creatures have -1 Naughty Points.\nAnyone with the Don't Mind Me Ability or the Boring or Angelic Countenance Quirks have -1 Naughty Points. Anyone with the Dark Demeanor or Unhinged Quirks have +1 Naughty Points.\nAttacking or using any Action or Ability to harm or Hinder Kranky Klaws gives +1 Naughty Points. Every Heart of Damage dealt to Kranky Klaws gives +1 Naughty Points. Using foul language gives +1 Naughty Points. Using any Action that Assists another creature without directly harming or hindering Kranky Klaws (such as the Tactical Assist Action or an Ability such as Compassion Cure for example) gives -1 Naughty Points.\nGiving an item to another creature or otherwise gifting them something gives -1 Naughty Points. GMs may give +1 or -1 Naughty Points for anything else they feel is appropriate.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Kranky Klaws has only ever been heard speaking Low Speech and only ever in a deep, booming voice. It is rumoured that he can understand every language, the better to judge how naughty or nice you've been according to his twisted ideals. Despite how popular the rumour is, few have survived an encounter with him and fewer still have tried to actually study this.\n",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Give Kranky Klaws a Murder Princess Ability or two to make him into a more deadly and more sinister variant. If doing so, consider adding Ailments to each result of the Bag Of Gifts table as well.\n\nReskinning some of the more whimsical aspects of Kranky Klaws can allow for a more serious Adversary, perhaps with a gambling theme. Bag Of Gifts for example could take the form of a deck of cards or handful of dice.\n",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Found all across the Outer World, but is always found in or around a festival. Any festival can draw him, but he seems to especially enjoy \"participating\" in gift-giving festivals.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Bloodied corpses with tattered wrapping paper nearby, booming laughter echoing from the distance, oddly despairing folk in the middle of an otherwise happy festival.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Kranky Klaws is jolly. Revel in the contrast between how jolly and friendly he acts and the horrific acts he commits. Kranky Klaws is never rude or aggressive. Even when dealing with those on the Naughty List or those he stuffs in his Bag, at worst he should speak like a loving grandfather scolding a naughty child.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "Kranky Klaws wears a Bright Red Suit with a white trim which acts as both Light Armour and an Extreme Weather Outfit (Cold). \n\nHe also wears a Bright Red Hat with a white trim that has a white ball on the end. When speaking the command words, \"You shall guide my slay tonight\" the ball glows red, acting as a lamp that requires no fuel and stays lit until the wearer wills it to turn off. \n\nBoth are sized for a Large creature so if someone smaller than this wishes to wear them they will need to have a Tailor who can make Advanced Items resize it.\n\nBag Of Gifts.\nWithout telling the players, keep their Hearts Total at the same value as when they defeated Kranky Klaws. When the Bag is first opened, a note falls out. If the players unfold the note it reads, \"Greedy children are Naughty children!\" The first time a player retrieves a Gift from the Bag, it will contain an Item that costs <75 Coins - something the player or character likes. A GMC taking a gift should receive a Treat. The second time a player takes a gift, roll on the table below.\n1-5 Normal Gift - Follow the same rules as above.\n6-15 Naughty Gift - Treat as a Grenade. The first Naughty Gift visibly damages the Bag. The second destroys it.\n16-20 Very Naughty Gift - Treat as a Bomb. This counts as setting the Bomb, so all characters have 1 Turn to act. This destroys the Bag.\n\nRemoving the bag from Kranky Klaws' back counts as setting a Bomb, giving the party 1 Turn to get out of the way before the bag and Kranky Klaws' body are destroyed in the explosion. When the Bag is destroyed or the party decide are done taking Gifts, return them all to maximum Hearts Total as normal at the end of Combat.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "tGIVRIsmYqiJZJ12mesz"
  },
