              "value": "1"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "hearts": {
        "current": 1,
        "tempMax": 0,
        "max": 1,
        "meterType": "hidden",
        "temp": 0
      },
      "actions": [],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "CynKKNlUupY0aNJMOZas",
          "name": "Eye Am Watching You [B].",
          "description": "- Immobile (No Speed Rating, treat as legs Restrained)\n- Any kind of Attack that hits will kill them. They cannot be non-lethally knocked out without some kind of sleeping spell, poison, or similar gentle method.\n- Can be picked up and moved by spending 1 Minute carefully removing them. A Might Check removes them quicker, but Failure will kill the Peeper. After picking one up, it will attach itself to anything its foot touches, so one must take care  brush its foot against their skin or clothing.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "ZqRXEnw1DdwTECF4uatN",
          "name": "Living Security System [B].",
          "description": "- Edge on any Insight Check or Contest relying on its eyesight, but automatically fails any Check or Contest that depends on the ability to hear, smell, touch or taste.\n- Can see in the dark and is immune to the Obscured Battlefield Condition caused by darkness. Unlike Underdwellers, they don't suffer a penalty in daylight.\n\nWhen they spot another Creature they begin to scream, creating the Obscured Battlefield Condition in the same Area for sounds only. It can also be heard from a long distance. Unless it is extremely large, assume that everything in the Adventure Site can hear it.\n\nProlonged exposure to the scream may require a Check to avoid the Deafened Ailment temporarily, with those with particularly good hearing suffering a Snag on the Check. The GM ultimately makes the call on how long counts as prolonged.\n\nThis screaming lasts until the Peeper can reasonably believe the Creatures have left the area, at least 1 Minute after it stops being able to see any creatures. It also tires itself out after screaming continuously for 10 minutes, which renders it unable to scream for an Hour. While screaming or tired out, it is Terrified, though as it's unable to move it cannot run away.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ],
      "speed-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "speed-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 0
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "allegiance": {
        "attributes": {
          "allegiance": {
            "dark-points": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": "1",
              "primary": true
            },
            "bright-points": {
