          }
        }
      },
      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Small",
        "name": "Peepers",
        "subname": "Rank 0 Mook",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Ear-splitting eyes. Deep in forgotten caves, it's easy to feel like you're being watched. The Peeper both proves this true. At first glance it'd be easy to mistake this bizarre creature for the eyestalk of some beast hiding beneath the ground. On closer observation, it's actually a whole creature affixed to the ground with a sticky foot, similar to some aquatic molluscs. Atop this sticky foot sits a slender, inky-black stalk topped with an eerily human-like eye.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 11
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 0
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Peepers have one tactic: scream until the creatures leave.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "It's not believed that Peepers are able to understand any speech, nor have they been observed making any sounds other than their infamous scream. It's possible they can communicate with others of their kind, but it's not presently understood whether this is possible and if it is, how they do this.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Some rare species of Peeper have a different sensory organ instead of an eye. Perhaps one is topped with an ear and has exceptional eyesight. Perhaps one has a nose and has an exceptional sense of smell. Perhaps one has some kind of mana-detecting organ.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "They are naturally found in many subterranean locations, though the Buried Kingdom has cleared out most of them from the locations they frequently pass through. Many dungeon-dwellers choose to relocate or even breed Peepers to act as living security systems, so it's not rare for a seemingly abandoned dungeon to have some. They can even live long after the creature that brought them there has moved away or died, as they feed on dust and other floating particulates.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "An ear-splitting scream that echoes throughout the location.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "They're just scared little creatures who think everything is out to kill them. Judging by how fragile they are, they're not far off.\n\nAt first glance it'd be easy to mistake this bizarre creature for the eyestalk of some beast \nhiding beneath the ground. On closer observation, it's actually a whole creature affixed to the ground with a sticky foot, similar to some aquatic molluscs. Atop this sticky foot sits a slender, inky-black stalk topped with an eerily human-like eye.\n\nOne shouldn't observe too closely however, as they have excellent eyesight and are very easily spooked. If they spot a potential threat, they give out an ear-splitting scream, which is often loud enough to be heard throughout the dungeon or cave system. For this reason, they're often cultivated as a kind of organic alarm by those who live in such isolated places. Their weakness however is that they entirely lack all senses other than sight. There are rumours of variants which lack sight but have a similarly exceptional other sense like hearing or smell.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "None, though some dungeon-dwellers may be willing to pay for a living Peeper to be relocated to a prime spot in their lair.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "uNO96m2eZsTEfm8zeoxF"
  },
