      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Small",
        "name": "Pum Kin",
        "subname": "Rank 1 Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Gourdy miscreants. Pum Kin are rowdy, mischievous and, sometimes, violent. They enjoy sneaking up on travellers and giving them a fright. Sometimes, especially when in groups, they take their pranks too far and attack. A rare taller variant, referred to as Jacks due to them all giving their name as Jack, are far less interested in pranks and are more likely to be intentionally malevolent.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 12
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 1
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Pum Kin are pranksters first and foremost. If they are alone, they will primarily use Combat Tricks to annoy their opponents without causing harm and are at worst an annoying pest and only resort to using their Kabocha Claws if their opponent also uses lethal force. In groups they are emboldened and use much more deadly tactics. In such situations they usually work in pairs, with one using Combat Tricks to harrass an opponent while the other scratches at them with their Kabocha Claws. If an opponent shows a good sense of humour, especially by pranking them back, they will often back off, laughing into the night.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "The Pum Kin primarily speak in Low Speech and seem completely disinterested in learning any other languages. There are the odd exception though, with Dark Tongue seemingly being favoured most often by those rare Pum Kin who bother to learn any other language.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Resize them to Medium and give them a Champion, Raider or Sneak ability to create the more dangerous and serious variant of Pum Kin - The Jacks.\n\nReplacing Hollow Head (and perhaps renaming Kabocha Claws) with something more appropriate you can easily reskin the Pum Kin into any small, mischievous creature. For example, replacing it with the Sneak's Light Footed Ability could create a monkey-like creature.\n",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Found all across Wistful Dark and some of the darker places in Twilight Meridian, they are mostly found in forests or other places with a large amount of vegetation. Sometimes they will invade a farm, pretending to be crops, waiting for the right time to jump out and surprise the farmers. There's no reason why they can't be found in other parts of the Outer World, but they prefer the dark due to it being better for sneaking around.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Ominous lights in the rough shape of a face, giggling come from the shadows, pranked travellers angrily or humiliatedly fleeing the scene.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "The Pum Kin have the temperament and motivations of naughty children. They generally don't want to fight, but a group mentality usually causes them to push their pranks into deadly territory. Even in these situations however, they can be distracted or impressed out of attacking. A sufficiently funny or interesting individual will usually draw their admirations. If they are in a friendly mood and are not in the process of pranking anyone, they may be convinced to trade for whatever trinkets they have stored in their heads.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "The Pum Kin rarely carry much, though sometimes they may store useful things, especially light sources, in their head. Some swear their flesh makes for a tasty, if mundane, ingredient for a wide variety of food.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "YLDBiW4KnyZlzVGXvF14"
  },
