      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: Skig",
        "size": "Small",
        "name": "Snatcher (Raccoon-Folk)",
        "subname": "Rank 0 Mook",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Snatchers are almost indistinguishable from large raccoons, often it is only the fact they are wearing clothes that gives them away. Snatchers are not above going naked to blend in with their raccoon friends, though they do prefer to be clothed, usually in loose trousers and a bandanna.\r\n",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 11
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 0
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Snatchers out scavenging usually pretend to be raccoons and run away if threatened. If cornered they will fight until they get a chance to run. \r\nWhen they do choose to fight, Snatchers favour dirty tricks. They usually gang up on one target if they can. They like to ambush people and will sometimes act like they are surrendering to give them a chance to get the jump with their concealed weapons. If there are raccoons present the Snatchers will act with genuine selfless courage to guard them should they be attacked and will fight with deadly fury if one is seriously hurt or killed.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Combat Gear",
          "id": "AdV2VUGGxlLp3oS0OFPO",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "description": "Concealed Weapon, Throwing Weapons. If they are expecting to fight they will often have Light Armour and a Small Shield.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "combat-gear",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Low Speech and a regional language. Can communicate with raccoons.\r",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Snatchers in bigger cities can be very well fed and may have the Girthsome Trait (Pg.136). Some bands of Snatchers prefer to mug rather than sneak around, these Snatchers swap out Trash Panda for Sticky Fingers (Pg.23)\r\n",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Snatchers like to live near settlements, usually on the outskirts or hidden in slum areas. Some groups do live in wild areas, where they prefer forests. They usually build a crude but defensible place to sleep, sometimes a burrow, sometimes a seemingly abandoned house, sometimes a little wooden fort. They always sleep in a single communal room, often with many normal raccoons.\r\nSnatchers are nocturnal and their natural aptitude for stealth, as well as their strong resemblance to raccoons, gives them an uncanny knack for living amongst other folk unnoticed.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Snatchers, or Raccoon-Folk, don\u2019t normally call themselves by those names, they just call themselves Raccoons and see normal raccoons as just another sort of the same thing, usually treating them like treasured younger siblings. They almost always live alongside raccoons (though they are a distinct species, they do not interbreed).\r\nNot usually violent, Snatchers love to steal. They usually sneak around at night rummaging through people's trash, but they also commit burglaries. They usually steal food or interesting things rather than targeting valuables. Most Snatchers don\u2019t really care for money and see legitimate commerce as stupid. Rural Snatchers are more inclined to foraging, but they still love to steal when they have the chance.\r\nWhen they think they are in danger snatchers will fight, but they usually only do so for as long as it takes to get a chance to run. Some groups do drift towards more active violence. When they feel that their home is threatened, Snatchers are much more willing to fight. They will also happily fight anyone who is cruel to raccoons.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "Snatchers always carry food, they will each have a Ration and 50% will have a Treat.\r\n",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "vRmHYaBAApinbBZ62Cdq"
  },
