      "actions": [],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "9943cFESn1ZsgdWZv9h5",
          "name": "Big'oop [B].",
          "description": "Being made of several goops, the supergoop is a Large creature (p.106).\r\n\u2022 +1 Might\r\n\u2022 -1 Defense rating\r\n\u2022 Can reach higher than other types of slimes and goops.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pgg9fugVeEUNi2mHtrUc",
          "name": "Colloid corpus [B].",
          "description": "Supergoops are from the same material as goops and undergo the same properties.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "lSkJNf1paNUUP8fAoxqZ",
          "name": "Inexorable sludge [B].",
          "description": "Supergoops are sticky and sluggish.\n\u2022 Their tacky surfaces allow them to traverse walls and ceilings.\n\u2022 Thanks to their greater size, Supergoops have an Average speed.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "9Q430fnMWj7O6Ff9Uu6f",
          "name": "Corrosive contact [B].",
          "description": "Caustic bodies destroy and consume. Work like the Goop ability, p. 383. You can use your Turn to attempt to remove a Supergoop (or rather, detach yourself from it). This requires a successful Might Check with a -2 penalty, for the Supergoop is bigger and stronger than regular goops.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "slV5v5V6Fn5wDCanSZFn",
          "name": "Multicreature [A].",
          "description": "The Supergoop is actually made of three Goops or so fused together in one body. Although they seem to share one will, each mind is distinct from the others.\n\u2022 Immune to Abilities and Ailments affecting the mind. One Goop might be affected, but the other keep control of the boy. The GM decides which Ailments may or may not affect the supergoop.\n\u2022 A Supergoop can use a Turn to disassemble and become three distinct Goops. It takes them one Turn to fuse and become a supergoop again.\n\u2022 Supergoops can restore one lost Heart by absorbing another Goop to replace the fallen one. It takes them an Action to absorb a new Goop into the colony and restore a Geart. Goops are usually not reluctent to join the colony.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ],
