              "value": 6
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "The Lonely runs headlong into the greatest concentration of enemies and attempts to Restrain two of them, switching to its Sorrowful Embrace once it has a Creature Restrained with each Arm. If enemies try to destroy its arms, it switches tactices, instead using its Branching Barbs whenever it is available and The Lonely has 2 Creatures Restrained.\n\nIf a single foe tries to leave its reach, The Lonely usually will attempt to attack to Restrain it and keep it from doing so, but if multiple Creatures seem to be triggering its abandonment weakness, it instead uses its Wretched Sobbing to keep them from fleeing.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
