      },
      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Medium",
        "name": "Toon Goon",
        "subname": "Rank 0 Mook",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Bizarre even for the Outer World, a Toon Goon resembles a drawing come to life. Indeed, this is exactly what they are. Some are brought to life through the scribblings of mad artists, others by particularly whimsical Unshaped, and others through even more bizarre methods.\n\nMischievous to the extreme, they live only to amuse themselves. Unfortunately, they have violent ideas of how to achieve this. Fortunately, their sheer whimsy reduces this violence to a non-lethal capacity. Unfortunately, this is still extremely humiliating.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 10
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 0
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Toon Goons have wildly different tactics that loosely depend on their appearance. One that resembles a soldier may use real weapons and armour (though they still inflict only slapstick injuries) while one that resembles an animal might fight with tooth and claw. Still others might produce objects such as custard pies or tomatoes from nowhere and pelt their unfortunate victims.\n\nWhatever the method of fighting, the only loosely consistent thing about them is they first attempt to fight in the funniest or most narratively-appropriate way, such as one resembling a Growl may first attempt to chase a Purr rather than fight the more dangerous opponents. Their ultimate aim would be to inflict a slapstick injury on every party member, after which they'll laugh, say some kind of catchphrase, then exit the scene.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Toon Goons understand Low Speech, but whether they can speak it varies wildly. Some can only communicate in squeaks or other noises which are inexplicably understood by other Toon Goons as though they're speaking. In fact, if their reactions are to be trusted, it would appear the incomprehensible ones are the most eloquent.",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "The sky's the limit! They can resemble almost anything, though keep it light-hearted. This also means you can freely select their size, remembering to alter their Attributes and Defence Rating. If their form has hands, they could wield weapons which may make them more dangerous.\n\nRank them up and select a Heretic Ability that they can perform without needing to make a Check to simulate being an escaped creation of a mad artist or perhaps the splitting if a Sealed Name from the one summoned by a failed Check by a Heretic. If they're at least Rank 6 they may have an Advanced Ability instead, though be careful not to make them too overpowered by remembering that these were balanced with risk in mind.",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "They're found throughout Outer World, though they're particularly drawn to locations with a large amount of whimsy energy. It's very common to find at least one near a Whimsy Stone.\n",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "The sound of goofy laughter, splotches of custard or other odd goop, the smell of ink or paint.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Reality is their plaything and boy are they im the mood for fun. Dial the whimsy up to 11 and channel zany Saturday morning cartoons.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "Mirthless Art Supplies.\nIf one is destroyed, they leave behind nothing but ink, paint, or whatever else they appeared to have been made of. Anyone who collects this feels as though whimsy is leaving their body or perhaps being drained from the area. There is no material effect of this, though the sadness or unease this brings about may feel very real.",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "2qraA9txuvWet1fqKPVa"
  },
  {
    "baseScale": 1,
    "groups": [
      "- adversaries [custom]",
      "boss"
    ],
    "privacy": {
      "level": "private",
      "users": [
        "HwYLq98tYuY9lEEODMru3sEGeTM2"
      ]
    },
    "activeSheet": "eDj3Wn10tM6E1nKzpC3T",
    "isActive": true,
    "name": "[1] Treat Tricker",
    "version": 9,
    "image": {
      "tokenCrop": {
        "unit": "%",
        "aspect": 1,
        "x": 25,
        "y": 25,
        "width": 50,
        "height": 50
      },
      "url": null
    },
    "sheetData": {
      "hearts-adversary": {
        "attributes": {
          "hearts-adversary": {
            "hearts-adversary-current": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": "2"
            },
            "hearts-adversary-max": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": "2"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "hearts": {
        "current": 2,
        "tempMax": 0,
        "max": 2,
        "meterType": "hidden",
        "temp": 0
      },
      "actions": [],
      "abilities": [
        {
          "id": "2QDZkszd33a5rzYTCeM0",
          "name": "Ethereal Body [B].",
          "description": "A Treat Tricker is a ghost and therefore follows different rules to the rest of reality.\n\nMay choose to ignore any non-magical material, such as walking through a wall or phasing through an attack.\n- Immune to mundane damage.\n- Takes -1 Dark Damage.\n- Takes +1 Bright Damage.\n- Destroyed instantly by direct sunlight, whether from the Sun Machine, a Star Gem or something else similar.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "dtAl3BDEzncdTqVnxCD3",
          "name": "Trick or Treat! [B].",
          "description": "The signature cry of the Treat Tricker, from which their name is derived. Both a greeting and a curse, this cry signals that you've been noticed by them. If you can give them a treat, they'll leave you alone. If you can't, well, you'll find out about their tricks.\n\nTarget must either place a Treat in the Treat Tricker's pail or succeed on a Grit or Aura Check, whichever is *lowest* to avoid being cursed.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "Eq02PaVI9njYKYKPDL1d",
          "name": "Boo! [B].",
          "description": "Treat Trickers have the temperament of a mischievous child and the powers of a ghost. The result is a very annoying spirit to deal with, though ultimately they're not dangerous.\n\nThey can become invisible at will. In Combat turning invisible or visible requires the use of their Action.\n\nWhen becoming visible, they may attempt to frighten a Target in the same Battlefield Area.\n\nRequires a Contest. Treat Tricker's Aura vs Target's Grit. On Success,the Target gains the Terrified Ailment, which lasts until the Target is sure the Treat Tricker is no longer nearby.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "id": "YB1XfjLJVKoKVjAcNAAT",
          "name": "Treat Tricker's Curse [B].\nRoll on the table below to determine exactly what curse falls on the unlucky victim. If the Target made a Check at all, then they're affected by it. If they succeeded on the Check then the effect lasts 1 Minute. If they Failed, then it lasts 24 hours or until it can be dispelled somehow. A Treat Tricker's love for Treats is too strong to simply be dodged!",
          "description": "1-10 - Cosmetic Catastrophe!\nThis prank has no mechanical effect on gameplay, but represents an embarrassing cosmetic change to the victim. Perhaps their clothing changes to garish colours,  their hair and eye colour swap, or their voice changes to sound like their grandmother's.\n11-13 - Phantom Raspberry!\nThe Treat Tricker personally haunts the victim. Every time they go to speak to someone, it appears behind them, blows a raspberry, then disappears. Inflicts a Minor Penalty on any Negotiation rolls.\n14-15 - All Thumbs!\nThe victim's fingers warp and transform into thumbs. Inflicts a Minor Penalty on any roll that requires the use of their hands.\n16-17 - Your Shoelace Is Untied!\nThis prank makes it difficult to move your feet. This might be in the form of your feet sticking to the ground, feeling incredibly heavy, or your shoelaces untying themselves whenever you're not looking. Inflicts a Minor Penalty on any roll involving the Target's feet.\n18-19 - Egg On Your Face!\nStuff keeps getting on your face, which makes it very difficult to notice anything else. Inflicts a Minor Penalty on any roll to look for, notice or otherwise use your eyes for a task. It probably also makes reading a huge pain, though if there's no roll involved this is more a cosmetic irritation.\n20 - Prank Gone Wrong. (Reroll if the Target succeeded on the Check to avoid the curse)\nWhatever the Treat Tricker was trying to do, they went too far or made a mistake in the execution, causing harm to the victim in some way. Target takes a Light Injury. The Treat Tricker appears immediately afterwards, very sheepish. They mumble an apology and give the Target a Treat to try to make up for it. The curse then ends immediately, though the Injury remains as normal.",
          "value": 0,
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ],
      "speed-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "speed-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 1
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "allegiance": {
        "attributes": {
          "allegiance": {
            "dark-points": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": "1",
              "primary": true
            },
            "bright-points": {
