      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: KeJoRo [Discord]",
        "size": "Small",
        "name": "Treat Tricker",
        "subname": "Rank 1 Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "Gluttonous ghost. At certain times of the year in the Wistful Dark spirits arise. These spirits spell trouble no matter what form they're in, though some are more dangerous than others. One common spirit that is more mischievous than dangerous is known as the Treat Tricker, so named by it's cry of, \"trick or treat\" before accosting its unlucky victim.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 11
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "wmm0Kj0nq98YFt1OMM9d",
            "itemId": "nla0piivyh2pUQPnROLY",
            "name": "Candy Pail",
            "description": "If one is destroyed, their pail is left behind. This is identical to any ordinary pail, though is usually stylised in a spooky or festive way. Inside it contains their haul of Treats. Roll 1d20 to determine how many.",
            "type": "none",
            "privacy": {
              "level": "public",
              "users": []
            },
            "creator": "",
            "data": {
              "cost": {
                "coins": 0
              },
              "encumbrance": 1.0
            },
            "version": 0,
            "owners": [],
            "quantity": 1,
            "equipped": false,
            "isCustom": true,
            "actions": []
          }
        ],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 1
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Treat Trickers do not want to hurt anyone. In fact, because they're sure they can neither hurt nor be hurt by their targets, they'll usually treat combat as a game. They will never initiate combat, being primarily interested in trying to gain Treats through Trick or Treat!, which they won't attempt during combat. If a victim takes offence and attacks them though, they'll play until they get bored. Their combat tactics consist of alternating between being visible and invisible, scaring their victims or using Combat Tricks to play pranks on them.\n\nThey delight in having weapons and other harmful things such as mundane fire pass through them. However, if anything manages to actually hurt them, such as a spell or a sword made of Magic Materials, they will react with fear, fleeing the battlefield in tears, exactly as a hurt child would.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Treat Trickers speak all the languages they spoke in life, which is usually Low Speech and one available to thise from Wistful Dark. Some particularly ancient ones nay not speak Low Speech though. Their advanced age does not come with increased maturity however.\n",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Grant them additional movement options or minor powers such as telekinesis to increase their options for pranks. Never give them anything lethal however, as they should always remain mischievous pests rather than legitimate threats.\n\nReverse the curse table for Trick or Treat! and remove the free Treat they hand out for causing an Injury to create a much more dangerous and malevolent spirit. Practice your evil (yet still mischievous) laugh!",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "They're found throughout the Wistful Dark, mostly in secluded alleyways or lonely roads between towns. While they are destroyed by direct sunlight, thus limiting them to the dark parts of the world, scholars have so far been unable to find out why they aren't found elsewhere, such as the Buried Kingdom for example. They are occasionally found in Night Haven though.",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "description": "Children giggling, a cold chill even on a still night, the signature cry of \"trick or treat!\"",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Indicators",
          "counters": {},
          "originId": "indicators",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "id": "OTg2GH2abw8CnphoYRBP",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "value": 0,
          "modifiers": [],
          "rollDetails": []
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "A mischievous child, dead and loving it. Remember that they're not just limited to human children, so bring some mannerisms and quirks from other Species in from time to time. A Gruun's idea of a prank will be very different from a Dwarf's for example.",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "S0P7E7RUTTb09LajhBIh"
  },
