      "bio": {
        "background": "Created by: Danov Valravn\r",
        "size": "Massive",
        "name": "Truck Kun",
        "subname": "Rank 6 Boss",
        "tokenCrop": "",
        "details": "A trope as old as time. A human gets hit by a truck and winds up in another world. Where does this truck come from? What plans does it have? Is it more of a force of nature? Now you can decide.\n\nIt's a truck that loves nothing more than punting folk back and forth across reality via a series of dimensional portals. Truck Kun is one of the reasons why so many lost and confused humans are appearing all over the place!\n\nThe Truck Kun seen on The Steam Isle has been witnessed playing what we assume is some kind of battle hymn called \"We Like to Party\" by the Vengaboys to intimidate foes and summon allies when threatened.",
        "appearance": "",
        "characteristics": {
          "height": "",
          "skin": "",
          "weight": "",
          "age": "",
          "eyes": "",
          "hair": "",
          "gender": ""
        },
        "profileImage": null
      },
      "defense-rating": {
        "attributes": {
          "defense-rating": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 14
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "inventory": {
        "maxEncumbrance": 0,
        "items": [],
        "currency": {}
      },
      "attack-bonus": {
        "attributes": {
          "attack-bonus": {
            "value": {
              "visible": true,
              "value": 4
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "description": "Truck Kun is a force of nature, so have him just doing something odd until the party decide to stop him, at which point he will generally do the following in roughly this order:\r\n- Summon help using \"We Like to Party\"\r\n- Sideswipe attack and try to get some distance\r\n- Use portals to create a shortcut across the battlefield\r\n- If they are definitely losing, try to escape through a portal to somewhere really random.",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "DBMa0akRFxeJjA4o7MVe",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "tactics",
          "counters": {},
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "modifiers": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "name": "Tactics",
          "value": 0
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "name": "Combat Gear",
          "id": "AdV2VUGGxlLp3oS0OFPO",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "description": "None. It's a truck.\r\n",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "originId": "combat-gear",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "counters": {},
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "description": "Blasting loud music, flashing its lights and honking its horn. Watch one of the old Herbie movies.\r",
          "name": "Communication",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "id": "Ntrz5p3hvUCRqLHi17zk",
          "originId": "communication"
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "id": "vhRuuxAZkiU0q109rpWa",
          "description": "Truck kun also doesn't really need to be a truck. Any kind of cargo hauling vehicle could be fair game.\r",
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "name": "Customization",
          "modifiers": [],
          "value": 0,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "originId": "customization",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "rollDetails": [],
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Habitat",
          "description": "Truck Kun can appear anywhere where there are roads.\r",
          "id": "cjG1nkOm4vkZPU7IEdlU",
          "originId": "habitat",
          "linkedValue": null,
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "Quick Facts",
          "value": 0,
          "linkedValue": null,
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "counters": {},
          "description": "Truck Kun is not evil, but it is absolutely an agent of chaos. Play up the light hearted mayhem, let it smash up everything, have portals drag your party (or NPCs you need to get a plot going) to wherever you want them to be. \r",
          "name": "Role Playing Notes",
          "counterOverrides": {},
          "rollDetails": [],
          "originId": "role-playing-notes",
          "id": "v0qTdpe9Mn52Vnrvpjar",
          "modifiers": []
        },
        {
          "value": 0,
          "name": "Yield",
          "rollDetails": [],
          "counters": {},
          "modifiers": [],
          "type": "Loot",
          "description": "As much random mechanical junk as the party can carry and use for crafting. Some random Other World \"cargo\". It could be bottled soda, it could be toilet roll, it could be novelty phone charms. Get weird with it!\n\n\nFinally, whoever has Truck Kuns fluffy dice can use them to create portals, however, when used by creatures that are not Truck Kun, they act as if cursed. For each time they are successfully activated by the party (Aura Check), roll on the following table:\n1-10: The portal goes where you want.\n11-14: The portal goes where you want, but is off by a couple of meters in whatever direction is the funniest/least helpful.\n15-18: The portal takes you somewhere random in the vague direction of where you wanted. Be that the wrong building, overshooting a city by several miles to a bandit den, directly into the centre of a bath house...\n19-20: The portal takes you where you need to go. Not where you want to go.... Destiny calls!",
          "modifiersPostCalculationFunc": null,
          "id": "RGRabawcHH0Dfexa8slm"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": "wWPEI4pZ4OO03KgRDs9X"
  },
